# Operation Rebuild

A strategy game set after the collapse of a technological civilization,
using D&D 5.2 SRD-style mechanics. Written in Perl 5.42+ with SDL3 and
Mooish::Base. Distribution name: `Game-OperationRebuild`.

Status: skeleton. The rules primitives (seeded random source, dice) exist;
the SDL3 interface and the server are stubs.

## Layout

- `bin/operation-rebuild`: graphical frontend (will autostart a local server)
- `sbin/operation-rebuild-server`: server with a text admin console
- `lib/`: all code; `lib/` stays unwoven in git
- `t/`: tests (Test2::V1); `xt/`: author tests
- `share/`, `etc/`, `doc/`: data, defaults, documentation

## Developing

Perl comes from `mise` (see `mise.toml`).

    mise run prove        # quick: prove -lr t, straight from lib/
    mise run test         # perl Build.PL && ./Build && ./Build test
    perl -Ilib bin/operation-rebuild --version

`./Build` weaves POD with Pod::Weaver into `blib/` only. Source files keep
their POD under `__END__`; NAME, VERSION, AUTHOR and LICENSE come from
`weaver.ini`, a `# ABSTRACT:` comment and `Build.PL`. `./Build dist` weaves
into the tarball, which does not need Pod::Weaver to install.

Use `--debug[=SEED]` on either program for a reproducible game (default
seed 42). Without it the seed comes from the clock.

See `INSTALL` for installation.

